From b3d7ad673d67775d770098ae14daf550ac85b7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:27:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] STD: add routing shim with sysctl, stats and boot param

Add kernel/sched/std.c and std.h above deadline. Fair and idle tasks
prefer housekeeping CPUs while deadline plus real-time tasks prefer
non-housekeeping CPUs. Intersect with p->cpus_ptr and fall back when
empty. Stop never intercepted. Pinned, migrate-disabled and
core-scheduled (rq-wide, may over-skip) pass through. EXT defers to
SCX. Guard small systems with fewer than three online CPUs.

Binary std_running: 1 enforcement (default, Cake-style deficit
sharing), 0 off (near-zero cost). Per-CPU 1024-entry 8-way flow table
(128 sets, pid/tgid/class hash, LRU) with base_quantum_ns ~1ms,
per-tin div_shift[8], sparse_thresh and decay_window tunables
(__read_mostly, no new sysctls). Fast path uses shifts only, no
alloc/float/do_div.

Enforcement denies cross-group only when in-group allowed exists,
else falls back; DL/RT imminent tasks bypass and count starve_bypass.
Per-CPU enforced/denied/starve_bypass counters extend the placement
counters to a 10-column bordered table with SI-1000 scaled values.
Rank is SMT-aware for funded flows: fully-idle core first via
cpu_smt_mask/topology_sibling_cpumask (NULL skipped, singleton
trivially passes; offline siblings ignored, not a veto), LLC-different
idle anchored at the class CPU via cpus_share_cache/cpu_llc_shared_mask
(both ifdef-guarded; on a single-LLC system no LLC-different CPU
exists, so this tier is a no-op falling through to tier 3), then any
idle; exhausted flows spread without piling (HK via distribute, non-HK
via distribute-like wraparound from a cpumask_any_distribute start, no
temp mask/alloc). Keeps deficit threshold, housekeeping mask,
cpu_active, available_idle_cpu and nr_cpu_ids fallback; no
alloc/lock/float/do_div.

Expose kernel.std_running 0644 minmax (0-1) and read-only
kernel.std_stats via register_sysctl_init and late_initcall. Stats
handler keeps the proc contract: ssize_t result, *lenp update,
return 0, -EROFS on write. Add std_running= boot param limited to
plain 0 or 1 (strict, no <bool> synonyms) plus kernel-parameters
documentation.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt |   4 +
 kernel/sched/std.c                              | 954 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel/sched/std.h                              |  66 ++
 3 files changed, 1024 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 kernel/sched/std.c
